It is Saturday morning.
I leave my flat.
On the stairs I meet Sabine and her small dog Bruno.
"Good morning, Maya!" says Sabine.
"Good morning, Sabine!" I answer.
"Are you going for a walk today?" she asks.
"Yes, I want to see the city today," I explain.
Sabine immediately has a good idea.
"Travel to Museum Island!" she says.
"The museums there are very interesting."
I ask her for the way.
"Don't take the U-Bahn," Sabine advises.
"Travel by tram instead."
"From the tram you see the city much better."
"The tram goes almost the whole way."
"Get off at the Hackescher Markt stop," she says.
"From there you only walk a short distance to the museums."
That is a great tip.
I thank her.
Then I go outside in my jacket into the cold.
